# OWNER REVIEW
# Councillor Swyne's cutaways (owner, 2026-11-14; Banjo's cuts back to the villain): after each world, the first time
# Nim's back at the club, the camera cuts to his office at City Hall after hours, the evening paper on his desk
# (levels/hub/swyne_office.gd). Three parts a world: <world> (pleased with himself), <world>_paper (what page two says,
# over a close-up of the paper), <world>_rage (working it out). He never believes he's the joke, and he always is.

~ pier
Swyne [pleased]: "Councillor Swyne condemned the filth on our seafront." Ha! Strong. Clear. They'll read that out in chapel.
Swyne: Now. Page two.

~ pier_paper
Swyne: "Pier manager found tied up in his own Prize Hall, wearing a rosette."

~ pier_rage
Swyne: Laffer. Somebody tied up Lou Laffer.
Swyne [angry]: And gave him a rosette! It says WINNER! He's never won a thing in his life. I made sure of it.
Swyne [angry]: Somebody is cleaning up my seafront. Cleaning up the seafront is MY campaign. I have the leaflets!

~ primrose
Swyne [pleased]: "The parish thanks Mrs. Gander for a record year." So it should. A pillar. A real pillar of the parish.
Swyne: And page two...

~ primrose_paper
Swyne: "...found tied to her own garden bench, beneath her own sign."

~ primrose_rage
Swyne [angry]: My sign. SWYNE FOR DECENCY. I paid for that sign! It was laminated!
Swyne: And her order book is missing. Every councillor's address is in that book. Every one.
Swyne [angry]: That's two. Somebody is reading my paperwork.
Swyne: I want those masks on every wall in the Old Quarter. WANTED. By morning.
